/-!
# Entry into one of several traps for 29 blocks whose sampled halves stay apart from their single traps

A trap passes the test of reach of [MissedTraps](MissedTraps.md) and still some half of the natural scan of its block
can sit, at step 12,000, inside a closed set of windows apart from it: no state of that set, cut to the narrower width,
is a state of the trap with a label of the same phase, so the half never enters ([what
failed](../../negative-results/columns/missed-traps.md)). For 29 blocks, 2 of period 11, 1 of period 12, 8 of period 13,
4 of period 14 and 14 of period 15, every trap of the trap modules is refuted so; but every node of the game of 20 cells
can reach one of the block's traps or of the natural traps its halves are inside, of 21 to 42 cells and 103 to 718
states. Here each block is reduced to entry into one of them, as the pairs of [TrapPairs](TrapPairs.md) are.

* `sets<block>_<k>`, with `_check` (and `_<part>`, `_parts` for the large ones): the natural traps, each passing the
  check of [WordTraps](WordTraps.md).
* `set<block>`, `set<block>_excludes`: the block's traps, those of its trap modules and the natural ones, and the
  reduction: if every finitely supported right half driven by the block enters one of them (`WTrap.AbsorptionSome`),
  the center column does not eventually repeat the block.

The tables come from `python -m computations.lock_chain --lean-trap-sets`. The natural-language argument is
`TrapSets.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata

